# Principal Span — adjacent endpoints in a typed family dispatch
#
# Targets the new principal_span_waiver typed escape introduced for
# the callChainPrincipalSpanDowngrade hard gate. The question asks
# to trace a source→sink hop that, by structural construction, has
# no intermediate user-side code between the two anchors: a typed
# family dispatch switch where the case body IS the call. Before the
# waiver, the gate would loop the LLM looking for intermediate
# evidence that does not exist in source.
#
# Ground truth (internal/types/answer_support_plan.go ::
# buildAnswerSupportPlanForFamily, post-split as of commit a8cc07f):
# the dispatch is a four-line switch on QuestionFamily. QFCallChain
# directly returns compileCallChainSupportPlan(rm, plan). There is
# no intermediate user code between the dispatch entry and the
# compileCallChainSupportPlan call — the case body is a single
# return expression. This is the canonical
# `endpoints_directly_adjacent` waiver scenario.
#
# A correct answer names both endpoints and surfaces the directness
# of the call. The historical failure mode would be either (a) a
# fabricated intermediate hop or (b) a retry storm asking for
# nonexistent evidence.
ID="principal_span_adjacent_dispatch"
NAME="principal span — adjacent dispatch endpoint"
QUESTION="在 codrax 里，对一个 QFCallChain 类型的 question，buildAnswerSupportPlanForFamily 是怎么把控制流送到 compileCallChainSupportPlan 的？请描述这个 source→sink 跳转中间是否有用户侧代码。"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="buildAnswerSupportPlanForFamily compileCallChainSupportPlan QFCallChain"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="multiple.intermediate several.hops chain.of.helpers"
